---------------------------------------------------------------------
PROSE SUMMARY (context, not a substitute for the structured log above)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
Long 30-turn grind, decided by deck-out rather than life loss. Campo's Jormuntide Ignis repeatedly attacked Inqory's Digtoise but was twice nullified by paid-Soul Dinossom interrupts (turns 5, 7) before finally destroying it turn 8, at the cost of Inqory's own board-wipe Lily's Strategy response. Both players leaned heavily on Pengullet explode-sacrifice plays to clear boards (turns 8, 9, 19, 28) while a steady stream of bare-form interrupts (Blazehowl, Foxparks, Cryolinx, Reindrix - turns 3, 10 x2, 14, 19, 21 x2, 29) and several paid/discarded full-form interrupts (turns 1, 5, 7, 18, 27) nullified attack after attack on both sides. Inqory's Cryolinx and twin Reindrix eventually ground Campo's life down (8->6->4->2, turns 16-23) via Pengullet Rocket Launcher buffed strikes and direct Reindrix hits, but Campo held at 2 life as the deck ran dry on turn 30, handing Inqory the win by deck-out.


